y/question-capture/14072443/assets/d6ee87bd861491394c6643679f62cb4b94436bf2777bd2436b3169e779736e2c.png)\n\nUsing the visual schematic above for the Cartesian product ${A}^{2}$ for $A={h,k},$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\n- ${h}^{2}\\in {A}^{2}$\n- $(h,k)\\in {A}^{2}$\n- $(k,k)\\in {A}^{2}$" 13194139535956 true] [17592186376515 1113 #uuid "79fb0aa2-93da-5faf-b8b1-c14f9fd9a036" 13194139535956 true] [17592186376515 1145 "The set ${A}^{2}$ is equivalent to the Cartesian product $A\\times A.$\n\nThe Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nTo complete our schematic of $A\\times A,$ we write an ordered pair whose first coordinate is the corresponding element of the first set $(A)$ and the second coordinate is the corresponding element of the second set $(A)$ at each intersection.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072443/assets/507f8f6306c309d5e894cfb1dabfc2019f371911f7878b196e1f329f1b37dfa6.png)\n\nAccording to our diagram:\n\n- ${h}^{2}\\in {A}^{2}\\,\\times $\n\n- $(h,k)\\in {A}^{2}\\,✓$\n\n- $(k,k)\\in {A}^{2}\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139535956 true] [17592186376516 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376517 13194139535956 true] [17592186376516 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376518 13194139535956 true] [17592186376516 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376519 13194139535956 true] [17592186376516 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376520 13194139535956 true] [17592186376516 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376521 13194139535956 true] [17592186376516 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535956 true] [17592186376516 1041 "selection" 13194139535956 true] [17592186376516 1104 #edb/ref 17592186376517 13194139535956 true] [17592186376516 1110 #uuid "9e4a7b22-0dec-5f23-80d6-3844ff0f3066" 13194139535956 true] [17592186376517 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535956 true] [17592186376517 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13